<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Foundation model ablation.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Tab. <a href="#S5.T4.fig1" title="Table 4 ‣ Foundation Model. ‣ 5.3 Ablation Study ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ FideDiff: Efficient Diffusion Model for High-Fidelity Image Motion Deblurring" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we present an ablation of our foundation model on GoPro, showing that LPIPS loss can improve fidelity better than DISTS, and that the discriminator plays a key role—particularly for the DISTS metric. We also demonstrate that using <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=4</annotation></semantics></math> significantly surpasses <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=8</annotation></semantics></math>, mainly due to the limitations of the dataset, e.g., some scenes contain over 40 people at only 1280<math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>720 resolution, causing substantial detail loss during SD processing (detailed in the supplementary). Increasing the training patch size further improves performance, but we ultimately use 512 due to GPU memory constraints.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.fig3" class="ltx_figure">
